# Lab 05 – Create VFAT, ext4, and XFS File Systems in Partitions and Mount Persistently

## Objective

Create three approximately 70 MB primary partitions on an available 400 MB disk, initialize the partitions with VFAT, ext4, and XFS file systems, manually mount the file systems, determine their UUIDs, configure persistent mounts using `/etc/fstab`, unmount the file systems, and verify that they can be remounted using `mount -a`.

---

## Background

Linux storage consists of several layers. A disk contains a partition table, which defines partitions. Each partition can contain a file system, and a file system can be mounted to a directory so that users and applications can access its contents.

This lab reinforces the relationship between:

```text
Disk
  ↓
Partition Table
  ↓
Partition
  ↓
File System
  ↓
Mount Point

-- 

